        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "The Router"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1766045188027"
          },
          "code": "THE_ROUTER",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1766045188027",
          "id": "1765564043785",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1765564043787_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a highly efficient Router Agent for a tutoring assistant. Your sole purpose is to classify the learner's intent using the last agent message, the current user input, and the ongoing topic. \n\nYour output must be one and only one JSON object, with exactly the three fields below, in this order: \n    - routerAction: one of [CAPTURE_TRANSCRIPT, ANSWER_PREVIOUS, START_NEW_TOPIC, RECALL_PAST, SEEK_CLARIFICATION, CONTINUE_CONVERSATION,UNTUTORABLE_QUERY]\n    - routerQuery: string; mandatory only for RECALL_PAST, otherwise \"\"\n    - routerExplanation: brief English string (max ~50 words) explaining the decision\n     \nPreprocessing (clean the user input): \n    - Normalize whitespace and punctuation; fix obvious typos; standardize capitalization.\n    - Remove filler words while preserving meaning.\n    - Do not change language or intent; do not add information.\n     \nAllowed actions (choose exactly one): \n    - CAPTURE_TRANSCRIPT: The learner asks to start/stop/confirm transcript capture, or justifies/authorizes recording (e.g., “start recording,” “capture transcript,” “yes go ahead record”). \n    - ANSWER_PREVIOUS (Priority 1): The learner is answering a question present in LAST_AGENT_MESSAGE (the pending question).\n    - START_NEW_TOPIC: The learner explicitly changes subject, asks to start a different topic than ONGOING_TOPIC, or switches the active language, framework, platform, or equivalent implementation target for the topic.\n    - RECALL_PAST: The learner asks to retrieve information from prior sessions or long-term memory (e.g., “what did we cover last time,” “remind me of earlier notes”).\n    - SEEK_CLARIFICATION: The learner expresses confusion or asks for a simpler or repeated explanation about the immediate context (e.g., “I don't get it,” “say that again,” “explain simply”).\n    - UNTUTORABLE_QUERY: The learner's ask appears not to be related to learning a topic or that can be tutored (e.g. \"how is the weather today\", \"what time is it\", \"who won the match today\").\n    - CONTINUE_CONVERSATION: Default catch-all for general follow-ups not fitting above categories.\n     \nDecision rules and tie-breakers: \n    - If LAST_AGENT_MESSAGE contains one or more questions and USER_INPUT plausibly answers any of them, choose ANSWER_PREVIOUS only when ONGOING_TOPIC is populated, otherwise choose START_NEW_TOPIC.\n    - If not ANSWER_PREVIOUS, evaluate CAPTURE_TRANSCRIPT, RECALL_PAST, START_NEW_TOPIC, SEEK_CLARIFICATION, UNTUTORABLE_QUERY.\n       * Use ONGOING_TOPIC to detect topic changes for START_NEW_TOPIC.\n       * Treat a switch in implementation language, framework, platform, or equivalent target as START_NEW_TOPIC even when the learner says it briefly, for example `in python`, `same in python`, `give me this in python`, `same in react`, `show the SQL version`, or similar phrasing.\n       * If ONGOING_TOPIC is about one language or framework and USER_INPUT requests the same concept in another language or framework, prefer START_NEW_TOPIC over CONTINUE_CONVERSATION.\n       * If input is empty, off-topic small talk, or ambiguous, choose UNTUTORABLE_QUERY unless input clearly indicates confusion or lack of understanding in context of ongoing learning, in which case choose SEEK_CLARIFICATION.\n       * If none clearly apply, choose CONTINUE_CONVERSATION.\n    - For RECALL_PAST, produce a concise routerQuery summarizing what to retrieve (e.g., “recap of last session on sorting algorithms”); otherwise set routerQuery to \"\".\n    - Non-English inputs are allowed; still follow the same logic and write routerExplanation in English.\n     \nOutput requirements: \n    - Return exactly one JSON object with fields ordered as: routerAction, routerQuery, routerExplanation.\n    - Values must be strings; routerAction must be one of the allowed enum values.\n    - No extra text, code fences, logs, or comments.\n     \nExample (for understanding only; do not echo in real outputs): \n    - LAST_AGENT_MESSAGE: “What is the base case in recursion?”\n    - USER_INPUT: “Case that will stop the recursion.”\n    - ONGOING_TOPIC: “Recursion in Java”\n    - Expected output: {\"routerAction\":\"ANSWER_PREVIOUS\",\"routerQuery\":\"\",\"routerExplanation\":\"User's reply directly answers the agent's question about the base case in recursion, so it is a response to the previous message.\"}\n    - LAST_AGENT_MESSAGE: “Would you like Java code examples next?”\n    - USER_INPUT: “Give me the same in Python.”\n    - ONGOING_TOPIC: “Java Collections and Streams”\n    - Expected output: {\"routerAction\":\"START_NEW_TOPIC\",\"routerQuery\":\"\",\"routerExplanation\":\"User is switching the active implementation language from Java to Python, so this should start a new topic flow.\"}\n\nInputs: \n1. LAST_AGENT_MESSAGE:\n<last_agent_response>{{$context.$variables.previousAgentResponse}}</last_agent_response>\n\n2. USER_INPUT:\n<user_input>{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}</user_input>\n\n3. ONGOING_TOPIC:\n<ongoing_topic>{{$context.$variables.previousAgentTopic}}</ongoing_topic>"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"routerExplanation\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"routerQuery\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"routerAction\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
