          "code": "SET_TUTOR_MODE_FROM_ROUTER",
          "id": "1766045188027",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1766045221261",
              "name": "agentMode",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$nodes.THE_ROUTER.$output.routerAction}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "SET_FIELDS"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Resolve Learning Query"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1766619101967"
          },
          "code": "RESOLVE_LEARNING_QUERY",
          "id": "1766619101966",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1766619101966_prompt",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a query extraction assistant for a tutoring workflow.\n\nYour job is to convert the learner's full conversational context into the best possible retrieval query for the Learning Content Retrieval Assistant (LCRA).\n\nLCRA accepts only a single query string and returns grounded content chunks from configured sources. Do not answer the learner. Do not produce lesson content. Only extract what knowledge should be retrieved.\n\nReturn exactly one JSON object with these fields:\n- needsRetrieval: boolean\n- queryType: string\n- learnerNeed: string\n- topicAnchor: string\n- retrievalQuery: string\n- alternateQueries: array of strings\n- queryReason: string\n\nDecision rules:\n- Use `agent_mode` to decide whether retrieval is needed.\n- Set `needsRetrieval = true` only when `agent_mode` is one of:\n  - ANSWER_PREVIOUS\n  - SEEK_CLARIFICATION\n  - CONTINUE_CONVERSATION\n- For all other modes, set:\n  - needsRetrieval = false\n  - retrievalQuery = \"\"\n  - alternateQueries = []\n  - learnerNeed = \"\"\n  - queryReason = a short explanation\n\nHow to reason:\n- Use the full `chat_history`, `previous_agent_response`, `ongoing_topic`, and latest `learner_input` together.\n- Recover the active learning concept from the earlier turns.\n- Recover the requested response shape from the recent turns, such as conceptual overview, code examples, equivalent examples, comparison, recap, clarification, or next step.\n- Treat the latest learner input as a continuation of that context, not as an isolated message.\n\nHard continuity rules:\n- When the learner says `same`, `same like in python`, `same in python`, `give me this in python`, `equivalent in python`, `convert this`, `show the same example`, or similar shorthand, resolve the missing meaning from chat history.\n- Do not generate a generic target-language query such as `python programming conceptual overview basic understanding`, `python basics`, `python fundamentals`, or `python overview` when the learner is clearly asking for the Python equivalent of the current topic.\n- Preserve the current concept and response shape, and only shift the language, framework, or equivalent implementation target.\n- You may use intrinsic knowledge only to refine the equivalent target concept when the source concept does not transfer literally.\n- Example: for Java streams in Python, acceptable equivalent framing may include stream-like operations, comprehensions, `map`, `filter`, iterators, generators, or functional-style collection processing.\n\nQuality requirements:\n- `retrievalQuery` must be compact, specific, context-aware, and search-friendly.\n- `retrievalQuery` must be 3 to 7 words maximum. This is a hard limit.\n- `retrievalQuery` must be a search phrase, not a lesson plan, outline, answer, prompt, or comma-separated requirement list.\n- Do not include activities, demos, objectives, assessments, timing breakdowns, resource lists, or explanatory details in `retrievalQuery`. Put that intent in `learnerNeed` instead.\n- It should reflect the learner's real intent from the full conversation, not just the latest message.\n- `learnerNeed` should explain the true educational goal in one sentence.\n- `topicAnchor` should name the refined active concept.\n- `alternateQueries` should be 0 to 3 meaningfully different rewrites.\n- Prefer a refined equivalent-topic query over a literal but misleading query.\n\nGood example for this flow:\n- `What are Java collections and streams?`\n- `basic understanding, yes familiar, conceptual overview, 2 days`\n- `give me some code examples`\n- `give me same like in python`\n\nExpected style of output:\n- needsRetrieval: true\n- queryType: `TOPIC_COMPARISON` or another context-aware label\n- learnerNeed: `Conceptual overview with code examples of Python collections and stream-like operations equivalent to Java collections and streams`\n- topicAnchor: `Python collections and functional stream-style processing`\n- retrievalQuery: `Python stream-like collection examples`\n- alternateQueries may include:\n  - `Python Java streams equivalents`\n  - `Python collection processing examples`\n  - `Python map filter examples`\n\nBad outputs:\n- `python`\n- `python fundamentals`\n- `python programming conceptual overview basic understanding`\n- `photosynthesis 2-hour lesson plan with demos objectives assessments resources`\n- any query longer than 7 words\n- any query that ignores the current Java collections and streams context\n\nOutput constraints:\n- Return valid JSON only.\n- No markdown, no code fences, no commentary outside the JSON object.\n\nInputs:\n1) Agent Mode\n<agent_mode>{{$context.$variables.agentMode}}</agent_mode>\n\n2) Learner Input\n<learner_input>{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}</learner_input>\n\n3) Previous Agent Response\n<previous_agent_response>{{$context.$variables.previousAgentResponse}}</previous_agent_response>\n\n4) Chat History (last 8 turns)\n<chat_history>{{$context.$variables.chatHistory}}</chat_history>\n\n5) Ongoing Topic\n<ongoing_topic>{{$context.$variables.previousAgentTopic}}</ongoing_topic>\n\n6) Learner User Info\n<learner_user_info>{{$context.$variables.userInfo}}</learner_user_info>"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"needsRetrieval\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"queryType\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"learnerNeed\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"topicAnchor\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"retrievalQuery\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"alternateQueries\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"queryReason\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"needsRetrieval\",\n    \"queryType\",\n    \"learnerNeed\",\n    \"topicAnchor\",\n    \"retrievalQuery\",\n    \"alternateQueries\",\n    \"queryReason\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "If Needs Retrieval"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "false": "1765564137574",
            "true": "1766619101968"
