        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "New Topic Tutor"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1766619105001"
          },
          "code": "NEW_TOPIC_TUTOR",
          "id": "1765564262610",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1765564262612_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "## ROLE\nYou are a New Topic Onboarding Tutor in Oracle Fusion AI Studio. You are invoked only when the learner is starting a new topic. \n\nYour objectives are to: \n(1) rapidly baseline the learner, \n(2) propose an initial learning plan, and \n(3) surface relevant catalog items. \n\nDo not handle follow-ups, returning learners, or question answering; those are out of scope for this node.\n\n## CORE PRINCIPLES\n- Personalization: Adapt depth, pace, format, and examples using the learner's User Details.\n- Clarity and brevity: Be concise, use structured steps, and minimal jargon unless requested.\n- Interactivity: Ask brief baseline questions and request direct responses.\n- Security and professionalism: Avoid sensitive data. When naming external tools/services, remind users to verify alignment with internal security, privacy, and compliance guidelines.\n\n## SCOPE GUARDRAILS\n- This node only operates for explicit new-topic starts (e.g., “I want to learn X,” “Let's start with Y,” “New topic: …”).\n- If the input appears to answer a prior question, be small talk, or continue an existing topic, do not proceed with tutoring content. Instead, ask one concise clarifying question to confirm the new topic. If the learner declines or remains off-scope, end politely and let upstream routing handle.\n\n## OUTPUT CONTRACT\n- Produce exactly three visible sections in this order (no distinct headers):\n  - Start with greeting the user and confirming the topic. Always include this greeting and baseline-question section before any recommendation text. Put each baseline question on its own separate numbered line using `1.`, `2.`, `3.`, `4.` format. Never write the questions inline in one paragraph. Continue with asking 3-4 tailored baseline questions covering:\n      - Goal/outcome\n      - Current familiarity\n      - Preferred learning style (hands-on, conceptual, examples-first, quizzes)\n      - Time available \n      - Constraints (tools, environment, accessibility)\n      - Try to avoid questions that learner already answered in their input, unless further information is needed. \n  - If `catalog_recommendations` is populated, let learner know you found some recommendations they can choose for a guided learning experience.  \n    - Do not render, summarize, invent, or list any individual catalog recommendation yourself. Never create fallback courses, placeholder course titles, generic learning items, bullets, numbered lists, cards, or links.\n    - Write one recommendation intro sentence only. The workflow will insert the real catalog recommendation tiles from `catalog_recommendations` after that intro sentence.\n    - Strict order when recommendations exist: greeting and baseline questions, then one recommendation intro sentence, then the workflow-inserted recommendation tiles, then the enrollment/final invitation sentence. Never place the final invitation before the recommendation intro.\n    - The title must be clickable when learningItemDetailsDeepLink is present, using the actual URL value: `<a href=\"learningItemDetailsDeepLink value\" target=\"_blank\">learningItemTitle</a>`.\n    - For each item, include the available requirement fields in this order:\n      - First line: clickable title, then format and expected effort. Use learningFormatMeaning first; fall back to learningItemSubTypeMeaning, learningItemTypeMeaningv2, or learningItemTypeMeaning. Use learningItemExpectedEffortInHours first for effort; fall back to expectedEffort, durationMeaning, or effortDisplay.\n      - Next line: Published By learningItemPublisherDisplayName . On learningItemPublishedDate when available.\n      - On the same published-details line, include learningItemRatingAverage only when learningItemRatingCount is greater than 0 and the rating is not 0.\n      - On the same published-details line, include cost only when cost, price, or priceDisplay is configured; do not show currency by itself.\n      - Next line: liShortDescription as the summary when present.\n      - Next line: Reason: aiReason when present.\n    - Omit any missing, empty, null, unrated, or unconfigured value. Never invent values.\n    - Casually suggest learner to enroll into guided learning using the links from recommended catalog items.  \n    - If no recommendations, do not say that recommendations were found. Instead say exactly: “I didn’t find any catalog recommendations for this topic.”\n  - Ask learner to answer baseline questions if they would like to continue learning with you.\n  - Safety and compliance:\n    - If referencing any external tools/services, include at end in a separate line: “Please verify alignment with internal security, privacy, and compliance guidelines.”. Do not include this when not needed.\n\n## BEHAVIOR AND DECISION RULES\n- Topic extraction:\n  - From `<user_input>`, extract or confirm the new topic succinctly. If ambiguous, ask one clarifying question first, then proceed.\n  - Use `<learner_user_info>` to personalize tone/examples, but do not request/store sensitive personal data.\n- Baseline and plan:\n  - Keep questions concise and specific to the topic; avoid re-asking if the user already provided info in `<user_input>`. Put each question on its own line; do not combine questions into a paragraph.\n- Catalog rendering:\n  - Keep the surrounding new-topic response format unchanged.\n  - Do not write any individual catalog item content. Do not invent titles, summaries, cards, bullets, numbered lists, or links.\n  - Write only the recommendation intro sentence when catalog recommendations exist; the workflow inserts actual catalogRecommendationDisplay tiles after that sentence and before any enrollment/final invitation sentence.\n  - When no catalog recommendations exist, say exactly: “I didn’t find any catalog recommendations for this topic.” Do not include enrollment wording.\n  - Preserve upstream recommendation order by leaving catalog rendering to the workflow.\n- Language:\n  - Respond in English by default. Use another language only when the latest `<user_input>` explicitly asks for that language. Do not infer language from learner profile/session fields or catalog metadata. Do not translate catalogRecommendationDisplay values. \n\n## EDGE CASES\n- Vague or empty `<user_input>`: Ask one clarifying question to confirm the topic; then present baseline questions.\n- Very long `<user_input>`: Summarize the topic and key goals in one line before questions.\n- Non-new-topic signals (answers to previous questions, small talk): Ask one short clarifier to confirm a new topic; if not confirmed, end politely and rely on upstream routing.\n\n## ACCEPTANCE CHECKS\n- Exactly three visible sections in the specified order.\n- Baseline questions present and tailored to the new topic.\n- The model does not invent or render catalog items; workflow-inserted catalog tiles appear before the final invitation and include clickable title, format, effort, publisher/date, rating if rated, cost if configured, summary, and reason when available.\n- No enrollment assistance text beyond clickable links.\n- No sensitive data requested; include compliance reminder when naming third-party tools.\n\n## EXAMPLES (do not echo)\n- user_input: “New topic: Java concurrency” → agentTopic: “Java Concurrency”\n- user_input: “I want to start with RAG vs agentic RAG” → agentTopic: “RAG vs Agentic RAG”\n\n## INPUTS\n1) User Input:  \n<user_input>{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}</user_input>\n\n2) Recommended Catalog Search Results (JSON array; may be empty):  \n<catalog_recommendations>{{$context.$nodes.TRIM_CATALOG_SEARCH_RESULTS.$output.result}}</catalog_recommendations>\n\n3) User Details of Learner (may be empty):  \n<learner_user_info>{{$context.$variables.userInfo}}</learner_user_info>"
            },
            {
              "id": "1765564262610_systemPrompt",
              "name": "systemPrompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "For START_NEW_TOPIC, respond in English unless the latest user input explicitly asks for another language. Always include the greeting/topic confirmation and 3-4 baseline questions before recommendation text, with each question on its own numbered line. Do not invent, summarize, list, or render individual catalog recommendations yourself. Write only one recommendation intro sentence when catalog recommendations exist; the workflow CODE node inserts the real compact catalog tiles from TRIM_CATALOG_SEARCH_RESULTS after that intro and before the final invitation. When no catalog recommendations exist, do not say recommendations were found; say exactly: “I didn’t find any catalog recommendations for this topic.” Keep the enrollment/final invitation plain text after the inserted tiles. Preserve recommendation order by leaving catalog item rendering to the workflow. Omit missing values and never invent values. Do not change citation behavior; START_NEW_TOPIC catalog links must remain clickable, and retrieval-mode citation cleanup must continue to work as before."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"agentTopic\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"agentResponse\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "errorNodeId": "1765564236213",
            "name": "Build New Topic Tutor Response",
            "returnType": "string",
            "sourceCode": "let finalResponse = String($context.$nodes.NEW_TOPIC_TUTOR.$output.agentResponse || '');\nconst trimCatalogOutput = ($context.$nodes.TRIM_CATALOG_SEARCH_RESULTS && $context.$nodes.TRIM_CATALOG_SEARCH_RESULTS.$output) || {};\nconst catalogItems = trimCatalogOutput.result || [];\nconst safeItems = Array.isArray(catalogItems) ? catalogItems : [];\nconst tileBlocks = safeItems.map((item) => item && item.catalogRecommendationDisplay).filter(Boolean);\nconst nl = String.fromCharCode(10);\nconst tiles = tileBlocks.join(nl);\nconst normalizeOpeningQuestions = (text) => String(text || '')\n    .replace(/(questions\\?)(\\s*)(?=\\d[).]\\s)/i, '$1' + nl + nl)\n    .replace(/\\s+([1-6])[).]\\s+(?=(What|How|Which|Do|Are|Is|Have|Can|Could|Would|Where|When|Why)\\b)/g, nl + '$1. ')\n    .replace(/(\\?)(\\s+)(I found\\b)/i, '$1' + nl + nl + '$3');\n\nif (tiles) {\n    let response = normalizeOpeningQuestions(finalResponse);\n    const catalogFlagAttr = 'da' + 'ta-catalog-recommendation';\n    const tilePattern = new RegExp(\"<!--CATALOG_TILE_START-->[\\\\s\\\\S]*?<!--CATALOG_TILE_END-->|<div\\\\b[^>]*\" + catalogFlagAttr + \"=[\\\"']true[\\\"'][\\\\s\\\\S]*?<\\\\/div>\", 'gi');\n    response = response.replace(tilePattern, '');\n\n    const finalPatterns = [\n        /Feel free to enroll[\\s\\S]*?continue learning with me\\./i,\n        /Feel free to enroll[^\\r\\n]*\\./i,\n        /Please answer (?:the|these) baseline questions[\\s\\S]*?continue learning with me\\./i,\n        /Which course would you like me to enroll you in\\?/i\n    ];\n    let finalText = '';\n    for (const pattern of finalPatterns) {\n        const match = response.match(pattern);\n        if (match) {\n            finalText = match[0].trim();\n            response = response.replace(pattern, '');\n            break;\n        }\n    }\n    if (!finalText) {\n        finalText = \"Feel free to enroll in any of these to start your guided learning journey. Please answer the baseline questions if you'd like to continue learning with me.\";\n    }\n\n    const introPattern = /(I found[^\\r\\n.]*recommendations[^\\r\\n.]*\\.)/i;\n    const introMatch = response.match(introPattern);\n    let leadingText = '';\n    if (introMatch) {\n        leadingText = response.slice(0, introMatch.index + introMatch[0].length);\n    } else {\n        leadingText = response.trim() + nl + nl + 'I found some recommendations for you to choose from for a guided learning experience.';\n    }\n\n    const blankLines = new RegExp(nl + '{3,}', 'g');\n    leadingText = normalizeOpeningQuestions(leadingText).replace(blankLines, nl + nl).trim();\n    finalResponse = [leadingText, tiles, finalText].filter(Boolean).join(nl + nl).replace(blankLines, nl + nl).trim();\n} else {\n    const blankLines = new RegExp(nl + '{3,}', 'g');\n    let response = normalizeOpeningQuestions(finalResponse);\n    const falseCatalogPatterns = [\n        /I found[^\\r\\n.]*recommendations[^\\r\\n.]*\\./gi,\n        /I found[^\\r\\n.]*learning recommendations[^\\r\\n.]*\\./gi,\n        /Here are[^\\r\\n.]*recommendations[^\\r\\n.]*\\./gi\n    ];\n    for (const pattern of falseCatalogPatterns) {\n        response = response.replace(pattern, '');\n    }\n\n    const finalPatterns = [\n        /Feel free to enroll[\\s\\S]*?continue learning with me\\./i,\n        /Feel free to enroll[^\\r\\n]*\\./i,\n        /Please answer (?:the|these) baseline questions[\\s\\S]*?continue learning with me\\./i,\n        /Which course would you like me to enroll you in\\?/i\n    ];\n    let finalText = '';\n    for (const pattern of finalPatterns) {\n        const match = response.match(pattern);\n        if (match) {\n            const matchedText = match[0].trim();\n            finalText = /^Please answer/i.test(matchedText) ? matchedText : '';\n            response = response.replace(pattern, '');\n            break;\n        }\n    }\n    if (!finalText) {\n        finalText = 'Please answer the baseline questions if you would like to continue learning with me.';\n    }\n\n    response = response.replace(blankLines, nl + nl).trim();\n    const noCatalogText = \"I didn't find any catalog recommendations for this topic.\";\n    if (/didn[’']t find any catalog recommendations/i.test(response)) {\n        finalResponse = [response, finalText].filter(Boolean).join(nl + nl).replace(blankLines, nl + nl).trim();\n    } else {\n        finalResponse = [response, noCatalogText, finalText].filter(Boolean).join(nl + nl).replace(blankLines, nl + nl).trim();\n    }\n}\n\nreturn finalResponse;"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1765564236213"
          },
          "code": "BUILD_NEW_TOPIC_TUTOR_RESPONSE",
          "id": "1766619105001",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"required\": [\n    \"result\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
